Company Description
 AUMOVIO fuhrt seit dem Spin-off im September 2025 das Geschaft des ehemaligen Continental-Unternehmensbereichs Automotive als eigenstandiges Unternehmen. Das Technologie- und Elektronikunternehmen bietet ein breites Portfolio fur eine sichere, begeisternde, vernetzte und autonome Mobilitat. Dazu gehoren Sensorlosungen, Displays, Brems- und Komfortsysteme sowie umfassende Expertise in Software, Architekturplattformen und Assistenzsystemen fur software-definierte Fahrzeuge. Die Geschaftsfelder, die nun zu AUMOVIO gehoren, erzielten im Geschaftsjahr 2024 einen Umsatz von 19,6 Milliarden Euro. Der Hauptsitz des Unternehmens ist in Frankfurt am Main. An uber 100 Standorten weltweit hat AUMOVIO rund 87.000 Beschaftigte.
 Job Description
 A DevOps Engineer Cloud Landing Zone is responsible for the development and operation of the globally used Secure Cloud Access (SCA) IT service.
 Key Responsibilities
 Landing Zone Engineering
Design, build and maintain a global cloud landing zone for Google Cloud Platform (GCP) and Amazon Web Services (AWS), following enterprise architecture, compliance and security standards;
Develop and enhance automated account/project/subscription provisioning and baseline configurations exclusively using Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC);
 Automation & Platform Enablement
Develop and maintain CI/CD pipelines for platform components;
Foster process automation to reduce manual work using GitHub Actions;
 Operations & Development
Operate and enhance the cloud platform with a strong focus on reliability and performance;
Drive incident resolution and root cause analysis in collaboration with other cross-functional teams;
Plan, coordinate and implement incoming platform changes for the further platform development;
 Collaboration and workstyle
Work within an agile global team using Scrum or Kanban;
Collaborate closely with internal and external teams on a global scale, e.g. security, network, governance and public cloud providers;
Participate in backlog refinement, sprint planning, retrospectives, and continuous improvement initiatives.
 Qualifications
Degree (e.g. business informatics, informatics) or comparable qualification;
Technical knowledge with at least one of the following cloud providers: AWS, Azure, GCP;
Competency with scripting languages such as Python;
Good knowledge of cloud networking (VPC/VNet design, DNS);
Good expertise about IT infrastructure components;
Strong proficiency in Infrastructure as Code (e.g. Cloud Formation or Terraform), CI/CD pipelines and DevOps tooling;
Agile methodologies (SCRUM);
Experience with AI usage (e.g. GitHub Copilot) highly recommended
Relevant certifications and/or experience in cloud computing, like: Solutions Architect Associate (AWS), Administrator (Azure), Associate Cloud Engineer (GCP);
Good team player with the ability to work in cross functional teams;
Strong problem-solving and analytical skills;
Fluent English skills, German skills helpful.
